{
  <section class="rich-lesson-section" data-g7-u09-l01 aria-label="Grade 7 Planning Recipes">
    <h3>Planning Recipes — Edulytiks</h3>
    <h4>Source-aligned project focus</h4><p>Use proportional reasoning to calculate per-serving nutrition and scale recipes. Reuse prior Grade 7 mathematical tools rather than creating a new mechanism for the culminating project.</p>
    <h4>Project connection</h4><p>Restaurant recipe planning and health-claim calculations. Machine Practice checks only closed calculation subresults; the project artifact and assumptions remain teacher reviewed.</p>
    <h4>Cool-down — first-party Edulytiks assessment</h4><p>A recipe makes 8 servings and contains 2,400 calories and 96 grams of protein in total. Find calories and protein per serving, then scale both totals to 14 servings and explain the proportional assumption.</p>
    <p><strong>Teacher review:</strong> Check model selection, assumptions, units, practical design or measurement method, and written justification. This Cool-down is independently authored. The local U09 student edition contains no separate lesson-practice page.</p>
  </section>
}

